Changes: the Lean files keep CompCert's names and only the definitions that the semantics of
this directory uses, without proof fields.  Machine integers are Lean's fixed-width words,
floating-point numbers are their bit patterns, and the numerical results of floating-point
operations come from Talos's integer implementation of IEEE 754 instead of Flocq, with NaN
results computed as Floats.v computes them.  Block contents are tree maps, and the parameters of
x86-64 and AArch64 that both targets share are fixed.  Rules for constructs outside the
translator's subset are omitted, and each file's header lists what it omits.  The other files of
LeanExe/Native/ are not derived from CompCert.
